Abstract

This document defines the Evaluation and Self-Improvement Model for the Memory Operating System.

The Evaluation Model defines how MOS measures:

outcomes,
decisions,
strategies,
capabilities,
communication,
resource efficiency,
reliability.

The Self-Improvement Model defines how MOS uses evaluation results to improve future cognition.

This RFC introduces the concept of the:

Cognitive Improvement Loop

where cognition continuously observes, acts, evaluates, learns, and evolves.

1. Purpose

Previous RFCs established the ability to act.

However, action alone does not create intelligence.

A system that executes the same mistakes repeatedly is not learning.

Therefore:

Every meaningful cognitive process must have an evaluation pathway.

2. Evaluation Axiom

MOS defines:

Every cognitive action SHALL produce measurable outcomes whenever evaluation is possible.

Example:

Decision:

Use retrieval strategy A

Outcome:

Accuracy:
92%

Latency:
200ms

Cost:
$0.02

The result becomes learning data.

